invariant: INV-36
file: chapulin.zig
catches: test/zig-build-check.sh
reason: the error table swaps CH_EPROTO and CH_EAUTH, so a chain the client
  refused reads as the peer breaking the protocol, and the reverse. Both
  leave the session dead, so nothing else notices. unit.zig's test of every
  code and loop_record.zig's impostor anchor, which expects error.Auth,
  object.

--- old
        error.Proto => c.CH_EPROTO,
        error.Auth => c.CH_EAUTH,
--- new
        error.Proto => c.CH_EAUTH,
        error.Auth => c.CH_EPROTO,
